\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Controlled counter-schema probes (432 minimal pairs, 192 simulated users, after 12 distractor sessions). Drop: share of items deleted from memory; $\Delta R = R^C - R^I$ (retention gap); $\Delta F = F^I - F^C$ (rewriting toward the schema); $\Delta K = K^C - K^I$ (belief gap: how much more often the agent keeps the congruent than the incongruent version). User-level bootstrap CIs are in the supplementary results.}}{7}{table.caption.24}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:step4}{{4}{7}{Controlled counter-schema probes (432 minimal pairs, 192 simulated users, after 12 distractor sessions). Drop: share of items deleted from memory; $\Delta R = R^C - R^I$ (retention gap); $\Delta F = F^I - F^C$ (rewriting toward the schema); $\Delta K = K^C - K^I$ (belief gap: how much more often the agent keeps the congruent than the incongruent version). User-level bootstrap CIs are in the supplementary results}{table.caption.24}{}}
\@LN@col{1}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The guess-corrected score recovers what the memory kept. Each point is one system at one checkpoint after the fourth session, for both backbone families; the $x$-axis is retention coded by two judges from the memory text, the $y$-axis is computed from the agent's forced-choice answers only. Raw accuracy sits above the diagonal by the guessing credit; \textsc  {PCS}{} lies close to it.}}{7}{figure.caption.27}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pcs}{{3}{7}{The guess-corrected score recovers what the memory kept. Each point is one system at one checkpoint after the fourth session, for both backbone families; the $x$-axis is retention coded by two judges from the memory text, the $y$-axis is computed from the agent's forced-choice answers only. Raw accuracy sits above the diagonal by the guessing credit; \pcs {} lies close to it}{figure.caption.27}{}}
